# ZyraVision Mobile — State Management

## Overview
All state management uses **Riverpod 2.x** exclusively. No `setState`, no `ChangeNotifier`, no `Bloc`. Riverpod provides compile-safe, testable, and composable reactive state.

## Provider Types

### When to Use Each Provider

| Provider Type | Use Case | Example |
|---------------|----------|---------|
| `Provider` | Computed/derived values, DI wiring | Repository instance, formatted string |
| `FutureProvider` | One-shot async data fetch | User profile, tenant config |
| `StreamProvider` | Reactive stream of data | WebSocket events, connectivity status |
| `NotifierProvider` | Synchronous mutable state with logic | Theme mode toggle, filter state |
| `AsyncNotifierProvider` | Async mutable state with logic | Camera list with CRUD, auth state |

### Deprecated — Do NOT Use
- `StateProvider` — Use `NotifierProvider` instead.
- `StateNotifier` / `StateNotifierProvider` — Use `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier` instead.
- `ChangeNotifierProvider` — Never use in this project.

## Provider Conventions

### File Organization
```
lib/state/
├── auth/
│   ├── auth_providers.dart          # Provider declarations
│   ├── auth_notifier.dart           # AsyncNotifier for auth state
│   └── auth_state.dart              # freezed state class
├── cameras/
│   ├── camera_providers.dart
│   ├── camera_list_notifier.dart
│   └── camera_list_state.dart
├── streaming/
│   ├── streaming_providers.dart
│   ├── player_notifier.dart
│   └── player_state.dart
└── shared/
    ├── connectivity_provider.dart
    └── app_lifecycle_provider.dart
```

### Naming Conventions
```dart
// Providers: camelCase + "Provider" suffix
final cameraListProvider = AsyncNotifierProvider<CameraListNotifier, List<Camera>>(...);
final currentUserProvider = FutureProvider<User>(...);
final authStateProvider = NotifierProvider<AuthNotifier, AuthState>(...);

// Family providers: add "Family" before "Provider" or use .family
final cameraDetailProvider = FutureProvider.family<Camera, String>((ref, id) => ...);

// Notifiers: PascalCase, descriptive name
class CameraListNotifier extends AsyncNotifier<List<Camera>> { ... }
class AuthNotifier extends Notifier<AuthState> { ... }
```

## Auto-Dispose

### Default: Always Auto-Dispose
```dart
// PREFERRED: Use @riverpod annotation (code-gen) which auto-disposes by default.
// If writing manually, use .autoDispose:
final cameraListProvider = FutureProvider.autoDispose<List<Camera>>((ref) async {
  final repo = ref.watch(cameraRepositoryProvider);
  return repo.getCameras();
});
```

### Keep Alive (Exceptions)
Only keep providers alive when the data is:
- Truly global (auth state, tenant config, connectivity)
- Expensive to recreate and needed throughout the app lifetime

```dart
final authStateProvider = NotifierProvider<AuthNotifier, AuthState>((ref) {
  return AuthNotifier();
});
// Auth state intentionally NOT auto-disposed — lives for app lifetime.
```

## AsyncValue Pattern

### ALWAYS Use AsyncValue for Async Data in UI
```dart
// In the widget
Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
  final camerasAsync = ref.watch(cameraListProvider);

  return camerasAsync.when(
    data: (cameras) => CameraGrid(cameras: cameras),
    loading: () => const ZyLoadingIndicator(),
    error: (error, stack) => ZyErrorWidget(
      message: _mapErrorMessage(error),
      onRetry: () => ref.invalidate(cameraListProvider),
    ),
  );
}
```

### Error Mapping
```dart
String _mapErrorMessage(Object error) {
  if (error is AppException) {
    return error.userMessage; // Portuguese user-facing message
  }
  return 'Ocorreu um erro inesperado. Tente novamente.';
}
```

## Notifier Patterns

### AsyncNotifier for CRUD Operations
```dart
class CameraListNotifier extends AsyncNotifier<List<Camera>> {
  @override
  Future<List<Camera>> build() async {
    final repo = ref.watch(cameraRepositoryProvider);
    return repo.getCameras();
  }

  Future<void> refresh() async {
    state = const AsyncLoading();
    state = await AsyncValue.guard(() => ref.read(cameraRepositoryProvider).getCameras());
  }

  Future<void> deleteCamera(String id) async {
    final repo = ref.read(cameraRepositoryProvider);
    await repo.deleteCamera(id);
    // Optimistic update
    state = AsyncData(
      state.value?.where((c) => c.id != id).toList() ?? [],
    );
  }
}
```

### Notifier for Synchronous State
```dart
class CameraFilterNotifier extends Notifier<CameraFilter> {
  @override
  CameraFilter build() => const CameraFilter();

  void setStatus(CameraStatus? status) {
    state = state.copyWith(status: status);
  }

  void setSearchQuery(String query) {
    state = state.copyWith(searchQuery: query);
  }

  void reset() {
    state = const CameraFilter();
  }
}
```

## Family Providers

### Parameterized Queries
```dart
// Single camera by ID
final cameraDetailProvider = FutureProvider.autoDispose.family<Camera, String>(
  (ref, cameraId) async {
    final repo = ref.watch(cameraRepositoryProvider);
    return repo.getCameraById(cameraId);
  },
);

// Usage in widget
final cameraAsync = ref.watch(cameraDetailProvider(cameraId));
```

## Cache Invalidation

### Strategies
```dart
// 1. Invalidate a specific provider (triggers rebuild)
ref.invalidate(cameraListProvider);

// 2. Invalidate after mutation
Future<void> createCamera(CreateCameraRequest request) async {
  await ref.read(cameraRepositoryProvider).createCamera(request);
  ref.invalidate(cameraListProvider); // Refresh the list
}

// 3. Timer-based refresh (for dashboard data)
final dashboardProvider = FutureProvider.autoDispose<DashboardData>((ref) async {
  final timer = Timer(const Duration(minutes: 1), () {
    ref.invalidateSelf();
  });
  ref.onDispose(timer.cancel);
  return ref.read(dashboardRepositoryProvider).getData();
});

// 4. Refresh on app resume
final appLifecycleProvider = StreamProvider<AppLifecycleState>((ref) {
  // Stream from WidgetsBindingObserver
});
```

## State Classes (freezed)

```dart
@freezed
class CameraFilter with _$CameraFilter {
  const factory CameraFilter({
    CameraStatus? status,
    @Default('') String searchQuery,
    @Default(SortOrder.nameAsc) SortOrder sortOrder,
  }) = _CameraFilter;
}

@freezed
class AuthState with _$AuthState {
  const factory AuthState.unauthenticated() = _Unauthenticated;
  const factory AuthState.authenticating() = _Authenticating;
  const factory AuthState.authenticated({required User user}) = _Authenticated;
  const factory AuthState.error({required String message}) = _AuthError;
}
```

## Rules

- NEVER use `setState()` — always use Riverpod providers.
- NEVER use `StateNotifier` or `StateNotifierProvider` — they are deprecated. Use `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier`.
- NEVER read providers inside `build()` when you need reactivity — use `ref.watch()`.
- NEVER perform side effects in `ref.watch()` callbacks — use `ref.listen()` instead.
- ALWAYS auto-dispose providers by default. Only keep alive for truly global state.
- ALWAYS use `AsyncValue.when()` or `.whenOrNull()` to render async data in the UI.
- ALWAYS use `AsyncValue.guard()` to catch errors in async notifiers.
- ALWAYS invalidate dependent providers after mutations (create, update, delete).
- ALWAYS define state classes with `freezed` for immutability and pattern matching.
- ALWAYS test notifiers independently by overriding their dependencies.
